   "timestamp": 1790347803612,
   "content": "The test suite still leaves temporary directories in /tmp. Eight test files were already fixed earlier today (afterEach/afterAll/try-finally with fs.rmSync); one `npm test` run still adds about 144 directories. Measured remaining offenders per run, by prefix: fuller-loop (about 56) and fuller-home (about 56), both created in tests/loop.test.ts; fuller-outside (about 10); fuller-evaltasks (about 5); fuller-diff-auto and fuller-diff-home (about 5 each); and a few others (fuller-mcp-*, fuller-del-home, fuller-fallback-home, fuller-agents, fuller-bg, fuller-img, fuller-extra, fuller-rules-*, fuller-trust-*, fuller-stream-*, fuller-robust-*, parity-*).\n\nTask: finish the cleanup.\n1. Start with tests/loop.test.ts: find where it creates the workspace and HOME directories (search for mkdtempSync in that file), and remove them after each test or after all tests with fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }). Keep the tests' behaviour.\n2. Then the other files that still create directories with the prefixes above without removing them. One grep for mkdtempSync in tests/ gives the list; check each file for an existing afterEach/afterAll/try-finally before changing it.\n3. Do not touch src/ and do not delete the directories that already exist in /tmp.\n4. Verify: `npm run typecheck`; then count `ls -d /tmp/fuller-* /tmp/parity-* 2>/dev/null | wc -l`, run `npm test`, count again, and repeat once more. Report the counts before and after each run, and the files you changed. A handful of directories left by processes killed mid-test is acceptable if you say which ones.",
   "tools": []
  },
